// Negative fixture: error recovery in the parser.
// Two *separate* missing semicolons, in two different functions. The parser
// is expected to report both in one run rather than stopping at the first,
// which is the parser-side half of the checklist's "Error Recovery" row
// (tests/sem_multi_errors.src is the semantic-analyser half).
//
// Recovery here is `many_rec`'s synchronize-and-skip: after a failed
// declaration it discards tokens up to the next statement or declaration
// boundary and resumes, so a mistake in `first` does not hide the one in
// `main`. tests/stray_brace.src pins the other property of the same
// combinator - that a token it cannot use still forces forward progress,
// so recovery terminates.
int first() {
    var int a = 1
    return a;
}

void main() {
    var int b = 2
    print(first(), b);
}
